  "summary": "Direct underwater monitoring at the Homathko Delta in Canada recorded fully submarine landslides that retreat slowly upslope, the signature of breaching failure. This had been hypothesized but never observed in nature. The slow failures also start lasting turbidity currents that carry sediment and carbon offshore. The observations come from a single delta, so other settings may behave differently.",
